INT. FAMILY COURT, HALLWAY BENCH - DAY

A scuffed corridor of benches and pay phones. Fluorescent hum.

ATTORNEY RENATA OKAFOR-LINDQVIST (40s, sharp) and ATTORNEY JULIAN BASHIR-MORRISSEY (40s, sharper) stand opposite each other, briefcases at their feet. Between them on the bench, a thick settlement envelope.

RENATA
Fifty-fifty.

JULIAN ^
Seventy-thirty.

RENATA
(together)
He gets the house and the dog.

JULIAN ^
(together)
She gets the house and the dog.

They stop. Look at each other. Look at the envelope.

RENATA
Neither of them has asked about the dog.

JULIAN
No.

Neither of them touches the envelope. Down the hallway, double doors swing open.

A bailiff steps out: BAILIFF CORNELIUS WEI (50s, uniform, clipboard).

CORNELIUS
Counsel. The judge will see you in chambers.

RENATA
Now?

CORNELIUS
Now.

Julian picks up the envelope. Renata picks up her briefcase. The bailiff holds the door. They walk through it together.

JULIAN
(low)
I want the dog.

RENATA
So do I.
